fact WorkItem(id: "WI-820", description: some(value: "Retire RuleId from the external read interface (057 R4). Goal: a fact read must not depend on whether the fact is memory-resident (has a RuleId) or extent-mounted (has none) — callers speak only values. read_facts / read_facts_resolved are already RuleId-free at the interface, and cpp-gen was fully migrated off RuleId-based reads (WI-771/810/774: no query_view/rule_head/rules_by_functor usage remains). REMAINING WORK: (1) shrink query_view to resolver-only — it returns (RuleId, Substitution) legitimately ONLY for SLD candidate selection (needs the rule BODY to open) and the CLI --match rule-browse; audit for any surviving READER (fact-shaped) caller and migrate it to read_facts/query_fact_heads, then ratchet query_view + head-as-answer enumeration to pub(crate) (057 R4). (2) Drive the Refuse->Resolve migration where a consumer can handle multi-valued/aggregated results, since Refuse is the TRANSITIONAL non-resolving candidate read and Resolve (read_facts_resolved) is the correct evaluate+aggregate read — the durable read primitive. cpp-gen's realization reads stay on Refuse until select_keyed / cpp_method_name can consume aggregated mappings (WI-774 deferred single-valued refinement). Relates 057, WI-773/806/810/771/774, WI-780 (write seam retires RuleId from resident storage, R3/R4)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-833", "WI-834"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "codex", at: "2026-08-10T10:00:58Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-820", name: "extent-seam")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-820", author: "user", content: "Classification after the CLI entry-discovery migration: anthill run uses read_facts_resolved for SortRequiresInfo, with regressions for a passing guard, a failing guard, and duplicate sorted providers. Remaining Refuse readers are deliberate: check/prove/todo read persisted source truth; stored-fact reads require stable FactRef; SMT must not admit guarded facts; C++ mapping needs explicit aggregation/select_keyed semantics; STL reflection cannot resolve until bootstrap paths provide declared field schemas and mutable KB access. No further safe Resolve migration remains in WI-820.", at: "2026-07-27T05:54:04Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-820", author: "user", content: "Closure audit: query_view and query_fact_heads are crate-private; the removed public query and query_rules reads are replaced by RuleId-free ProgramClauseMatch snapshots for program browsing. No external fact-shaped reader depends on RuleId. Resolve migrations cover CLI SortRequiresInfo entry discovery and C++ realization mappings; the remaining Refuse readers are deliberate source-truth, stored-fact identity, SMT soundness, aggregation, or bootstrap cases, so no further safe migration remains in WI-820. Full rustland/scripts/test.sh passed: 35 test results, 4475 passed, 0 failed, 11 ignored. Manual code review found no WI-820 findings; the repository-required /code-review skill was unavailable in this session and therefore was not run.", at: "2026-08-10T10:00:53Z")
